    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0448" n="436" xml:id="pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/31063: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-09T13:00:00+03:25">September 9,
                            1943—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 10—9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>927. My 914, September 3.<anchor n="89a" xml:id="d458-f1"/> Shah by Royal Firman
                    signed this morning at 9:34 declared war on Germany. Medjliss later in morning
                    approved the declaration by vote of 73 out of 77 Deputies present. Foreign
                    Minister has requested Swiss Chargé in Tehran to request his Government to
                    endeavor to effect departure from Germany within 30 days of all Iranians
                    residing there. Iranian Government is instructing Minister in Washington
                    approach Department with regard to Iran’s adherence to United Nations
                    Declaration. Summary of Prime Minister’s speech in Medjliss will be telegraphed
                    as soon as translated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For exchange of telegrams between the Secretary of State and the Iranian
                        Minister for Foreign Affairs concerning the declaration of war by Iran on
                        Germany, etc., see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, September 18, 1943, page 180.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
